  "semantic_caveats": [
    "Each fixed seed resets Python, NumPy, and Torch RNGs, but batched categorical sampling consumes the Torch stream in a different order from scalar sampling, so trajectories and decision counts are distribution-comparable rather than pairwise identical.  The vector engine also partitions deck randomness into one independent stream per game.",
    "The canonical differential suite separately proves exact rules, deck, hand-order, duplicate, terminal, and truncation equivalence under deterministic decisions across 128 seeds.",
    "Compiled CUDA updates have a large one-time graph-build cost. Cold workers use fresh temporary compiler caches; warm workers run one unmeasured update, restore model/optimizer/scaler state, and reset RNGs before measurement. Short runs can use --no-compile_updates.",
    "Rollouts use the requested device and the critic uses CUDA; CUDA allocated memory excludes driver/context reservations."
